decision: changes-requested

Four blockers remain:

- **N1 — high:** [validate_carry.go:107](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go#L107) relies on `git diff --name-only`, which omits a rename’s source path. Moving `a/required.txt` to `b/required.txt` can select only `b` and carry `a`’s old pass despite its required file disappearing. Include both rename endpoints and test this sequence.
- **N2 — high:** [validate_scope.go:135](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go#L135) exempts self-contained modules after ownership matching fails. A root module `"."` never matches ordinary paths such as `main.go`, so its own changes can be carried. Handle root-module ownership explicitly.
- **N3 — high:** [validate_scope.go:83](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go#L83) parses Git’s quoted, newline-delimited filenames as literal paths. A changed filename containing non-ASCII characters, quotes or newlines can lose its module ownership; the new self-contained exemption then carries that affected module. Use NUL-delimited path parsing.
- **N4 — medium:** [validate_carry.go:184](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go#L184) gives different dirty builds at the same revision the identical `<version>+<revision>.dirty` identity. Eligibility can therefore carry results across engine changes, contradicting D2. Reject unverifiable dirty engine identities or bind them to their actual build content.

These findings follow from code inspection; new reproduction fixtures could not be created because scratch storage is read-only.

Prior **R1-F1 is fixed**: the dirty-base regression passes. Focused carry, selection, delivery/material-binding tests, focused race tests, and `go vet` passed. The module validation failed on sandbox write restrictions. Global validation reached 181 passes before cancellation. The supplied sealed matrix passes, but my required-tool runs did not establish a fresh passing gate.

Rules applied: review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. Reviewed bundle `rvb-b0296611766ddddc`; the design assessment reproduced sealed digest `design-b9c442f12ae40005`. No files changed or attestation was recorded.

